{{Politics of the Czech Republic}}

Presidential elections were held in the [[Czech Republic]] in January 2018. The first round took place on 12 and 13 January. As no candidate won a majority, a [[Two-round system|run-off election]] between the top two candidates, [[Jiří Drahoš]] and President [[Miloš Zeman]], was held on 26 and 27 January 2018.

In the first round, voters chose between nine candidates who qualified for the elections either by gathering 50,000 signatures from the public, 10 signatures from [[Senate of the Czech Republic|Senators]] or 20 signatures from [[Member of Parliament#Czech Republic|members]] of the [[Chamber of Deputies of the Czech Republic|Chamber of Deputies]] (MPs). Incumbent president Miloš Zeman, running for re-election for his second and last term, finished first with 38.57%, followed by former president of the [[Czech Academy of Sciences]] Jiří Drahoš, who received 26.60%.

In the second round, Miloš Zeman narrowly defeated Drahoš and was elected for a second term in office. Voter turnout was 66.60%, the highest since the [[1998 Czech legislative election|1998 legislative elections]].

==Background==
Former prime minister Miloš Zeman was elected as [[President of the Czech Republic]] in [[2013 Czech presidential election|2013]], defeating Minister of Foreign Affairs [[Karel Schwarzenberg]] in the country's first direct presidential elections. Until 2012, all presidential elections in the Czech Republic were [[Indirect election|indirect]], with the president being chosen by the [[Parliament of the Czech Republic]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://zpravy.e15.cz/prezidentske-volby-2018|title=Prezidentské volby 2018|website=Zprávy E15.cz|access-date=2017-12-12}}</ref>

According to polls conducted in 2016, Zeman was the front-runner and his chances of re-election were considered high,<ref>{{cite web|title=ANALÝZA: Zemanovy šance na obhajobu zvyšuje soupeření Babiše se Sobotkou|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/zemanovy-sance-na-obhajobu-zvysuje-soupereni-babise-se-sobotkou-px8-/domaci.aspx?c=A161221_125103_domaci_kop|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=1 January 2017|date=21 December 2016}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|title=Miloš Zeman válcuje soupeře|url=http://www.denik.cz/z_domova/milos-zeman-valcuje-soupere-20160628.html|website=Deník.cz|access-date=1 January 2017|date=28 June 2016 |last1=Perknerová |first1=Kateřina }}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=Průzkum: Zeman jasně vede. Horáček druhý|url=http://www.parlamentnilisty.cz/arena/monitor/Pruzkum-Zeman-jasne-vede-Horacek-druhy-440103|website=parlamentnilisty.cz|access-date=1 January 2017}}</ref> although it was speculated that Zeman's candidacy would be determined by his health.<ref>{{cite web|title=Bude Zeman znovu kandidovat? Víme, co rozhodne|url=http://www.reflex.cz/clanek/komentare/76027/bude-zeman-znovu-kandidovat-vime-co-rozhodne.html|website=Reflex.cz|date=21 November 2016 |access-date=1 January 2017}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=Průzkumy i sázkové kanceláře se mýlily v případě Trumpa i Hofera. Je dobré teď vsadit na Zemana?|url=http://www.reflex.cz/clanek/komentare/76439/pruzkumy-i-sazkove-kancelare-se-mylily-v-pripade-trumpa-i-hofera-je-dobre-ted-vsadit-na-zemana.html|website=Reflex.cz|date=10 December 2016 |access-date=1 January 2017}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=Echo24.cz má prý zprávy z Hradu, které Zemanovy fanoušky nepotěší. Týkají se kandidatury v příštích volbách|url=http://www.parlamentnilisty.cz/arena/monitor/Echo24-cz-ma-pry-zpravy-z-Hradu-ktere-Zemanovy-fanousky-nepotesi-Tykaji-se-kandidatury-v-pristich-volbach-466587|website=parlamentnilisty.cz|access-date=1 January 2017}}</ref> Zeman announced his candidacy on 9 March 2017.<ref>{{cite web|title=Miloš Zeman oficiálně oznámil kandidaturu na prezidenta|url=http://zpravy.e15.cz/domaci/politika/milos-zeman-oficialne-oznamil-kandidaturu-na-prezidenta-776543|website=Zprávy E15.cz|access-date=28 March 2017}}</ref> There was speculation that both the [[Czech Social Democratic Party|Social Democrats]] (ČSSD) and [[ANO (political party)|ANO]] may endorse Zeman,<ref name="Miloši, Miloši!">{{cite web|title=Miloši, Miloši! Premiér Sobotka to prý zkouší na Zemana, protože se bojí Babiše. Noviny slyšely více|url=http://www.parlamentnilisty.cz/arena/monitor/Milosi-Milosi-Premier-Sobotka-to-pry-zkousi-na-Zemana-protoze-se-boji-Babise-Noviny-slysely-vice-469615|website=parlamentnilisty.cz|access-date=3 January 2017}}</ref> but neither party did in the end. Some commentators speculated that Zeman could be elected in the first round.<ref>{{cite web|title=Paroubek: Kdyby se dnes volil prezident, Zeman vyhraje v prvním kole|url=http://www.ceskatelevize.cz/ct24/domaci/1692823-paroubek-kdyby-se-dnes-volil-prezident-zeman-vyhraje-v-prvnim-kole|website=ČT24|access-date=18 April 2017|language=cs}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|last1=Honzejk|first1=Petr|title=Jiné čtení průzkumů: Co když Zeman vyhraje už v prvním kole?|url=http://archiv.ihned.cz/c1-65698270-zeman-miri-k-vitezstvi-uz-v-1-kole|website=Hospodářské noviny|access-date=18 April 2017|language=cs|date=18 April 2017}}</ref>

On 23 August 2017, the Speaker of the Senate announced that the first round would be held on 12 and 13 January 2018, with a second round being held on 26 and 27 January 2018, if required.<ref>{{cite web|title=Češi si začnou volit prezidenta 12. ledna. Předseda Senátu vybral dřívější termín|url=http://www.lidovky.cz/sef-senatu-stech-ve-stredu-oznami-presny-termin-prezidentske-volby-11t-/zpravy-domov.aspx?c=A170823_080610_ln_domov_ELE|website=Lidovky.cz|access-date=23 August 2017|date=23 August 2017}}</ref> The deadline for nominating candidates was scheduled for 7 November 2017.<ref>{{cite web|title=Češi budou volit prezidenta 12. a 13. ledna|url=https://www.novinky.cz/domaci/447051-cesi-budou-volit-prezidenta-12-a-13-ledna.html|website=Novinky.cz|date=23 August 2017 |access-date=23 August 2017|language=cs}}</ref>

==Candidates==
In order to qualify for the ballot, candidates must gather 50,000 signatures from citizens, or the support of twenty [[Chamber of Deputies of the Parliament of the Czech Republic|Deputies]] or ten [[Senate of the Parliament of the Czech Republic|Senators]]. The candidates must file their applications and signatures 66 days before the election, following which the [[Ministry of the Interior (Czech Republic)|Interior Ministry]] will verify a sample of the signatures.<ref name=signs>{{cite news |url= http://praguemonitor.com/2012/08/02/klaus-signs-direct-presidential-election-bill |title= Klaus signs direct presidential election bill |agency= [[Czech News Agency]] |work= [[Prague Daily Monitor]] |date= 2 August 2012 |access-date= 21 September 2012 |url-status= dead |archive-url= https://archive.today/20130201040841/http://praguemonitor.com/2012/08/02/klaus-signs-direct-presidential-election-bill |archive-date= 1 February 2013 |df= dmy-all }}</ref>

19 candidates submitted themselves as candidates.<ref>{{cite web|title=O post prezidenta se chce utkat 19 kandidátů, někteří budou nejspíše z boje vyřazeni |url=https://zpravy.e15.cz/volby/prezidentske-volby-2018/o-post-prezidenta-se-chce-utkat-19-kandidatu-nekteri-budou-nejspise-z-boje-vyrazeni-1339554|website=Zprávy E15.cz|access-date=10 December 2017}}</ref> Only nine of them met requirements for registration and became official candidates: [[Jiří Drahoš]], [[Pavel Fischer]], [[Petr Hannig]], [[Marek Hilšer]], [[Michal Horáček]], [[Jiří Hynek]], [[Vratislav Kulhánek]], [[Mirek Topolánek]] and [[Miloš Zeman]].<ref>{{cite web |title=O prezidenta může usilovat jen 9 lidí, zbylé přihlášky vnitro vyřadilo |author=<!-- no byline -->|url=https://echo24.cz/a/puHS8/o-prezidenta-muze-usilovat-jen-9-lidi-zbyle-prihlasky-vnitro-vyradilo |website=Echo24.cz|access-date=10 December 2017|language=cs|date=10 November 2017}}</ref>

=== Official candidates ===
Nine candidates gathered the required number of signatures and had their candidacy approved by the [[Ministry of the Interior (Czech Republic)|Ministry of the Interior]]. Candidates are listed according to number allocated by the Ministry.<ref>{{cite web|title=Vylosovaná čísla, kterými budou označeny hlasovací lístky pro volbu prezidenta republiky |url=http://www.mvcr.cz/clanek/vylosovana-cisla-kterymi-budou-oznaceny-hlasovaci-listky-pro-volbu-prezidenta-republiky.aspx|website=Czech Ministry of the Interior|access-date=20 December 2017|language=cs}}</ref>
