==Debates==
{{main|2018 Czech presidential election debates}}
[[Czech presidential election debates, 2018|The first debate]] was held on 8 November 2017 at [[Charles University]], and included Jiří Drahoš, Michal Horáček, Marek Hilšer, Jiří Hynek, Pavel Fischer, Petr Hannig and Mirek Topolánek. [[Miloš Zeman]] refused to participate and instead went to meet with citizens in the Olomouc region.<ref>{{cite web|last1=Cápová|first1=Michaela|title=První souboj prezidentských kandidátů. Podívat se přišel Babiš i Tonda Blaník|url=https://echo24.cz/a/pKkja/prvni-souboj-prezidentskych-kandidatu-podivat-se-prisel-babis-i-tonda-blanik|website=Echo24.cz|access-date=8 November 2017|language=cs|date=8 November 2017}}</ref> Topolánek called for defense of the [[Schengen Area|Schengen border]]. Drahoš stated that he wanted respect for the rules.<ref>{{cite web|title=PŘÍMÝ PŘENOS: Musíme hájit vnější schengenskou hranici, řekl Topolánek|url=https://zpravy.idnes.cz/debata-kandidatu-na-hrad-pravnicka-fakulta-fim-/domaci.aspx?c=A171108_125220_domaci_kop|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=8 November 2017|date=8 November 2017}}</ref> The moderator mentioned Drahoš's attack against Topolánek, to which Topolánek stated that "it was either written by a woman or a PR Mage. I forgave the Professor, whether I ever took it seriously." The audience was allowed to vote for who they liked the most. Drahoš and Hilšer received the most votes.<ref>{{cite web|title=Hrad by to chtělo vydezinfikovat, řekl Horáček v debatě kandidátů|url=https://www.novinky.cz/domaci/454421-hrad-by-to-chtelo-vydezinfikovat-rekl-horacek-v-debate-kandidatu.html|website=Novinky.cz|date=8 November 2017 |access-date=8 November 2017|language=cs}}</ref> According to [[Hospodářské noviny]], Topolánek and Hilšer came across as the most civil candidates.<ref>{{cite web|last1=Wirnitzer|first1=Jan|title=V první debatě kandidátů na prezidenta bodoval Drahoš, Topolánek bavil. Zeman mezitím vedl nepřiznanou kampaň na Olomoucku|url=http://archiv.ihned.cz/c1-65949270-v-debate-kandidatu-na-prezidenta-bodoval-drahos-topolanek-bavil-zeman-mezitim-vedl-nepriznanou-kampan-na-olomoucku|website=Hospodářské noviny|access-date=9 November 2017|language=cs|date=8 November 2017}}</ref>

Seznam News held a presidential debate on 13 November 2017. Topolánek, Drahoš, Horáček, Fischer, Hilšer and Kulhánek participated. Topolánek was considered the winner of the debate.<ref>{{cite web|title=Prezidentští kandidáti debatovali na Seznamu. O Rusku i Zemanovi|url=https://www.seznamzpravy.cz/clanek/prezidentsti-kandidati-debatovali-na-seznamu-o-rusku-i-zemanovi-39796|website=Seznam Zprávy|date=13 November 2017 |access-date=13 November 2017}}</ref> Another debate was held in Liberec on 16 November 2017.<ref>{{cite web|title=Latentní rasismus v nás je, řekl Topolánek v debatě kandidátů na Hrad|url=https://zpravy.idnes.cz/prezidentska-debata-liberec-osm-kandidatu-fip-/domaci.aspx?c=A171116_173218_domaci_kop|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=17 November 2017|date=16 November 2017}}</ref>

==Opinion polls==
{{main|Opinion polling for the 2018 Czech presidential election}}
Opinion polls from 2014 showed Miloš Zeman leading in the first round with between 20% and 48% of the vote. Michal Horáček became his main rival during 2016 but was overtaken by Jiří Drahoš during 2017. Drahoš was leading polls for the second round with a 10% lead in September 2017. The margin narrowed during October and November and Drahoš' lead fluctuated between 0.5% and 4%. Some polls in late January 2018 showed Zeman with a narrow lead.

