==Aftermath==
Zeman said that a narrow victory pleases the most people, and that he respected all people who vote. Zeman confirmed that his second term would be the end of his political career, as the election was "his last political victory that won't be followed by any political defeat."<ref>{{cite web|title=Zeman slaví těsnou výhru, volební účast byla rekordní|url=https://www.tyden.cz/rubriky/domaci/politika/zive-zeman-prijima-gratulace-dostal-51-36-procenta-hlasu_464810.html|website=TÝDEN.cz|access-date=30 January 2018|date=27 January 2018}}</ref> Drahoš conceded defeat and congratulated Zeman. He stated that he would not be leaving politics, telling supporters: "We didn't win but we didn't lose. I want to use the huge amount of energy that shouldn't disappear".<ref>{{cite web|title=Drahoš pogratuloval Zemanovi. Ve veřejném životě zůstane|url=https://www.euro.cz/prezidentske-volby-2018/drahos-uznal-porazku-ve-verejnem-zivote-zustane-1391878|website=Euro.cz|access-date=30 January 2018|language=cs|date=27 January 2018}}</ref>

Prime Minister [[Andrej Babiš]] congratulated Zeman and said that he had believed that the campaign based on attacks against him could not succeed.<ref>{{cite web|title=Gratulace z domova i ze zahraničí. Zemanovi poblahopřál Putin i Kiska, Brusel mlčí|url=https://www.irozhlas.cz/volby/prezidentske-volby-2018-milos-zeman-reakce-gratulace_1801280810_ako|website=iROZHLAS|date=28 January 2018 |access-date=30 January 2018|language=cs}}</ref> Leader of the opposition [[Petr Fiala]] also congratulated Zeman, and expressed hope that Zeman would serve the interests of the Czech Republic. The leader of Pirate Party, [[Ivan Bartoš]], stated that he was pleased about the strong support for Jiří Drahoš. SPD leader [[Tomio Okamura]] and acting Social Democrat leader [[Milan Chovanec]] celebrated the results with Zeman at his election headquarters. Okamura expressed joy at the result, and Chovanec stated that he was glad that Zeman won. Communist Party leader [[Vojtěch Filip]] described Zeman's victory as an assurance of stability. KDU–ČSL leader [[Pavel Bělobrádek]] expressed hope that Zeman would unify the divided society. [[Miroslav Kalousek]] expressed dissatisfaction with the result and stated that the Czech Republic had wasted an opportunity for change.<ref>{{cite web|title=Fiala gratuloval Zemanovi, doufá, že bude sloužit zájmům ČR|url=http://www.ceskenoviny.cz/zpravy/fiala-gratuloval-zemanovi-doufa-ze-bude-slouzit-zajmum-cr/1578710|website=ceskenoviny.cz|access-date=30 January 2018|language=cs}}</ref> Zeman was also personally congratulated by his predecessor [[Václav Klaus]]. Klaus stated that he was glad about the result but afraid that Drahoš' supporters would not accept it. Zeman thanked Klaus for his support and invited him for a drink.<ref>{{cite news|title=Klaus přišel pogratulovat Zemanovi. Obává se, že poražení výsledek nepřijmou|url=https://www.denik.cz/z_domova/volby-2018-klaus-prisel-pogratulovat-zemanovi-20180127.html|website=Deník.cz|access-date=30 January 2018|language=cs|date=27 January 2018}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=Klaus přišel blahopřát Zemanovi. Obává se, že poražení výsledek nepřijmou|url=https://www.novinky.cz/domaci/461759-klaus-prisel-blahoprat-zemanovi-obava-se-ze-porazeni-vysledek-neprijmou.html|website=Novinky.cz|date=27 January 2018 |access-date=30 January 2018|language=cs}}</ref>

By the end of February 2018, the [[Supreme Administrative Court of the Czech Republic|Supreme Administrative Court]] rejected all of about 70 complaints concerning the regularity of elections, ruling that there were no serious mistakes or violations of the election law that could have influenced the outcome of the election.<ref name="soud">{{cite news|title=Zvolení Zemana je definitivní, soud zamítl všechny stížnosti|url=https://echo24.cz/a/Sdmt2/zvoleni-zemana-je-definitivni-soud-zamitl-vsechny-stiznosti|access-date=7 March 2018|work=Echo24.cz|agency=Czech News Agency|date=21 February 2018|language=cs}}</ref> Some of the rejected complaints were then submitted to the [[Constitutional Court of the Czech Republic|Constitutional court]], which rejected the last complaint in June 2018, thus confirming the result.<ref name="tecka">{{cite news |title=Definitivní tečka za prezidentskými volbami. Ústavní soud zamítl stížnost kvůli registraci uchazečů |url=https://www.irozhlas.cz/zpravy-domov/prezidentske-volby-registrace-ustavni-soud_1806111024_pj |access-date=7 September 2018 |work=iROZHLAS.cz |agency=Czech News Agency|publisher=Český rozhlas |date=11 June 2018 |language=cs}}</ref>

According to a poll conducted by Median, 54.2% of Czech people were satisfied with the result, and 37.5% were dissatisfied.<ref>{{cite web|title=Průzkum: Zeman vyhovuje velké části nevoličů. Drahoš byl přijatelný jen pro každého desátého|url=https://www.lidovky.cz/zeman-vyhovuje-velke-casti-nevolicu-ukazuji-volebni-pruzkumy-p7a-/noviny.aspx?c=A180129_220511_ln_domov_ele|website=Lidovky.cz|access-date=30 January 2018|language=cs|date=30 January 2018}}</ref>

===International reactions===
*{{flag|China}} - President [[Xi Jinping]] congratulated Zeman and stated that he wants to take the strategic partnership between the two countries to a higher level.<ref>{{cite web|title=Čínský prezident pogratuloval Zemanovi ke znovuzvolení a nabídl upevnění strategického partnerství|url=https://www.irozhlas.cz/zpravy-svet/cina-prezident-milos-zeman-gratulace_1801281239_pj|website=iROZHLAS|date=28 January 2018 |access-date=30 January 2018|language=cs}}</ref>
*{{flag|European Union}} - European Commission President [[Jean-Claude Juncker]] congratulated Zeman and said he was looking forward to working with him. European Council President [[Donald Tusk]] also congratulated Zeman on his victory.<ref>{{cite web|title=Zemanova blahopřání z čela EU. Ke znovuzvolení mu pogratulovali Juncker i Tusk|url=https://www.lidovky.cz/zemanovi-blahoprali-celni-predstavitele-eu-juncker-a-tusk-pn3-/zpravy-domov.aspx?c=A180129_180914_ln_domov_ele|website=Lidovky.cz|access-date=30 January 2018|language=cs|date=29 January 2018}}</ref>
*{{flag|France}} - President [[Emmanuel Macron]] congratulated Zeman on 13 February 2018, and highlighted the friendly relations and historical ties between the two countries.<ref>{{cite web|title=Hrad: Prezident republiky obdržel gratulaci od francouzského prezidenta|url=https://www.parlamentnilisty.cz/zpravy/tiskovezpravy/Hrad-Prezident-republiky-obdrzel-gratulaci-od-francouzskeho-prezidenta-524197|website=Parlamentní Listy|access-date=13 February 2018}}</ref>
*{{flag|Germany}} - President [[Frank-Walter Steinmeier]] congratulated Zeman and noted the two countries' common history.<ref>{{cite news|title=Zemanovi pogratuloval německý prezident i Putin. Merkelová nereagovala|url=https://www.denik.cz/ze_sveta/volby-2018-zemanovi-pogratuloval-nemecky-prezident-i-putin-spojene-staty-mlci-20180129.html|website=Deník.cz|access-date=30 January 2018|language=cs|date=29 January 2018}}</ref> Chancellor [[Angela Merkel]] congratulated Zeman on 1 February 2018.<ref>{{cite web|title=Hrad: Prezident republiky obdržel gratulaci od Angely Merkelové|url=https://www.parlamentnilisty.cz/zpravy/tiskovezpravy/Hrad-Prezident-republiky-obdrzel-gratulaci-od-Angely-Merkelove-522610|website=Parlamentní Listy|access-date=13 February 2018}}</ref>
*{{flag|Israel}} - Prime Minister [[Benjamin Netanyahu]] personally congratulated Zeman.<ref>{{cite web|title=Zeman jmenoval soudce se zpožděním. Izraelský premiér se nepřerušuje, vysvětlil|url=https://www.novinky.cz/domaci/462069-zeman-jmenoval-soudce-se-zpozdenim-izraelsky-premier-se-neprerusuje-vysvetlil.html|website=Novinky.cz|date=31 January 2018 |access-date=31 January 2018|language=cs}}</ref>
*{{flag|Russia}} - President [[Vladimir Putin]] was among the first to congratulate Zeman, saying that the election confirmed Zeman's authority. He expressed readiness for constructive cooperation on bilateral relations.<ref>{{cite news|last1=Krupka|first1=Jaroslav|title=Putin gratuloval Zemanovi, podle něj prosazuje touhy českého národa|url=https://www.denik.cz/ze_sveta/volby-2018-putin-gratuloval-zemanovi-podle-nej-prosazuje-touhy-ceskeho-naroda.html|website=Deník.cz|access-date=30 January 2018|language=cs|date=28 January 2018}}</ref>
*{{flag|Slovakia}} - Prime Minister [[Robert Fico]] was the first international politician to congratulate Zeman, calling him an intelligent and experienced politician and saying that he was pleased with the result.<ref>{{cite news|last1=Krupka|first1=Jaroslav|title=Fico gratuloval Zemanovi k obhájení prezidentského mandátu|url=https://www.denik.cz/ze_sveta/fico-gratuloval-zemanovi-k-obhajeni-prezidentskeho-mandatu.html|website=Deník.cz|access-date=30 January 2018|language=cs|date=27 January 2018}}</ref> President [[Andrej Kiska]] congratulated Zeman and expressed hope that relations between the two countries would stay close. He also invited Zeman to Slovakia.<ref>{{cite web|title=Fico je rád, že vyhral Zeman. Kiska ho pozval na Slovensko|url=https://slovensko.hnonline.sk/1682959-fico-je-rad-ze-vyhral-zeman-je-inteligentny-a-skuseny-politik|website=HN Online|date=27 January 2018 |access-date=30 January 2018|language=sk}}</ref>

===Analysis===
Observers compared the presidential race to previous elections such as the [[2016 Austrian presidential election|2016 Austrian]],<ref>{{cite web |first= Cyrille |last= Bret |title=Czech presidential election: A vote on Europe |url=http://neweasterneurope.eu/2018/01/23/czech-presidential-election-vote-europe/ |date=23 January 2018 |publisher=[[New Eastern Europe]] |access-date=28 January 2018}}</ref><ref name="Reuthers">{{cite news |first1= Jan |last1=Lopatka |first2=Robert |last2=Muller |title=Openness or protection? Czechs' choice echoes EU, U.S. votes| url=https://www.reuters.com/article/us-czech-election-president/openness-or-protection-czechs-choice-echoes-eu-u-s-votes-idUSKBN1F42H0| date=15 January 2018 |work=[[Reuters]] |access-date=28 January 2018}}</ref> [[2016 United States presidential election|2016 United States]]<ref name="Reuthers"/><ref name="Politico"/><ref name="CNN"/><ref>{{cite news |title=Czech Presidential Election Headed for Tight Run-Off Vote -Poll |url=https://www.reuters.com/article/us-czech-election-president-poll/czech-presidential-election-headed-for-tight-run-off-vote-poll-idUSKBN1FA0P2 |date=21 January 2018 |work=[[Reuters]] |access-date=27 January 2018 |quote=The Jan. 26-27 second round echoes other elections in the past two years across the European Union as well as U.S. President Donald Trump’s battle with former Secretary of State Hillary Clinton for the White House in 2016.}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |first=Ciaran |last=McGrath|title=Czech election latest: Zeman plots to hold on to presidency against pro-EU Drahos |url=https://www.express.co.uk/news/world/905167/EU-Czech-election-Zeman-Drahos-migrants-migration-run-off|date=15 January 2018 |newspaper=[[Sunday Express]] |access-date=28 January 2018 }}</ref><ref name="BBC"/> and [[2017 French presidential election|2017 French]]<ref name="Reuthers"/><ref name="Politico"/> presidential elections, which saw a [[Liberal internationalism|liberal internationalist]] running against a [[national populist]].<ref name="Politico">{{cite web |last=Mortkowitz |first=Siegfried |title=Prague's Turn for Populist Vs. Liberal Showdown |url=https://www.politico.eu/article/milos-zeman-jiri-drahos-czech-election-prague-turn-for-populist-vs-liberal-showdown/ |date=26 January 2018 |website=[[Politico Europe]]|access-date=27 January 2018}}</ref><ref name="CNN">{{cite web |last1=McKenzie |first1=Sheena |title=Why the Czech Presidential Election is One to Watch |url=https://www.cnn.com/2018/01/26/europe/why-czech-presidential-election-matters-intl/index.html |date=26 January 2018|publisher=[[CNN]] |access-date=27 January 2018}}</ref><ref name="BBC">{{cite news |last1=Cameron |first1=Rob |title=Czech Election: Milos Zeman Wins the Battle of Ideas |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/world-europe-42848835 |date=27 January 2018 |work=[[BBC News]] |access-date=27 January 2018}}</ref><ref name="ideas">{{cite web|last=Cameron|first=Rob|title=Milos Zeman vote settles Czech presidency - or does it?|url=https://www.bbc.com/news/world-europe-42848835|website=BBC News|access-date=29 January 2018|date=27 January 2018}}</ref> Though both sides seemed to have roughly equal support among Czech voters, the national populism was represented by clearer ideology and strong leaders, while the liberal message was fragmented and the candidates did not have common themes or language, apart from agreeing on the need for an "anti-Zeman" candidate.<ref name="Pečinka">{{cite web|last1=Pečinka|first1=Bohumil|title=Drahoš mohl vyhrát, ale Zeman podal výkon na hranici svých možností. Komentář Bohumila Pečinky|url=http://www.info.cz/volby/prezidentske-volby-2018/drahos-mohl-vyhrat-ale-zeman-podal-vykon-na-hranici-svych-moznosti-komentar-bohumila-pecinky-23161.html|website=Info.cz|access-date=28 January 2018|language=cs|date=28 January 2018|trans-title=Drahoš could win, but Zeman pushed his performance to the limit.}}</ref><ref name="Boček">{{cite web|last=Boček|first=Jan|title=Tři analýzy: Drahošovi se nepodařilo získat voliče poražených v 1. kole, ztratil i vlastní příznivce|url=https://www.irozhlas.cz/volby/volic-jiri-drahos-milos-zeman-vysledky-volby-prezident-analyza_1801281010_jab|website=iRozhlas.cz|publisher=[[Czech Radio]]|access-date=28 January 2018|language=cs|date=28 January 2018|trans-title=Three analyzes: Drahoš failed to win voters of opponents defeated in the first round, he further lost his own fans}}</ref><ref name="Fér">{{cite web|last=Fér|first=Ondřej|title=Prezidentské volby 2018 skončily, je čas začít myslet na ty, které budou možná už za rok|url=http://www.info.cz/volby/prezidentske-volby-2018/prezidentske-volby-2018-skoncily-je-cas-zacit-myslet-na-ty-ktere-budou-mozna-uz-za-rok-23132.html|website=Info.cz|access-date=28 January 2018|language=cs|date=28 January 2018|trans-title=The 2018's presidential election is over, it's time to start thinking about those that may come next year}}</ref>

According to analysts, important factors in Zeman's victory were his strong debate performances and the closeness of the first round results, the latter helping mobilize his base. Drahoš was estimated to have lost about a quarter of his voters as a result of the televised debates.<ref name="Boček"/><ref>{{cite news|first=James|last=Shotter|title=Milos Zeman Wins Second Term as Czech President | url=https://www.ft.com/content/dbd93060-036d-11e8-9650-9c0ad2d7c5b5 | date=27 January 2018 | newspaper=[[Financial Times]] | access-date=27 January 2018}}</ref><ref name="HowEuroTrump"/> Analysts also pointed out that the support for Zeman came from districts with high levels of [[poverty]], and also from regions dominated by traditional industries, [[agriculture]] and the [[construction industry]], while regions dominated by [[Information technology|IT services]] and [[public administration]] supported Drahoš.<ref name="Boček"/><ref name="sociolog">{{cite news|last1=Wirnitzer|first1=Jan|last2=Šrajbrová|first2=Markéta|title=Ještě v pondělí vedl Drahoš. Rozhodl poslední týden a Zemanova mobilizace, říká sociolog Prokop|url=https://zpravy.aktualne.cz/domaci/volby/volby-rozhodl-posledni-tyden-a-zemanova-mobilizace-rika-soci/r~a3275c58039311e89704ac1f6b220ee8/|access-date=28 January 2018|website=Aktuálně.cz|publisher=Economia|date=28 January 2018|trans-title=On Monday Drahoš was still winning. It was the last week and Zeman's mobilization what decided, says sociologist Prokop|language=cs}}</ref> Zeman's strident opposition to immigration also worked in his favor,<ref name="HowEuroTrump">{{cite web | last1=Mortkowitz | first1=Siegfried | title=How (the European) Trump Won a Second Term | url=https://www.politico.eu/article/milos-zeman-czech-republic-how-the-european-donald-trump-won-a-second-term/ | date=28 January 2018 | website=[[Politico Europe]]| access-date=28 January 2018}}</ref><ref>{{cite news | last1=Muller | first1=Robert | last2=Hovet | first2=Jason | title=Czech President Zeman Re-Elected With Anti-Immigration Message | url=https://www.reuters.com/article/us-czech-election-president/czech-president-zeman-re-elected-with-anti-immigration-message-idUSKBN1FG00C | date=26 January 2018 | work=[[Reuters]] | access-date=27 January 2018}}</ref> though his major opponents Drahoš and Horáček also voiced opposition to immigration and the EU's migrant quotas, while all but one candidate criticised illegal immigration to Europe.<ref name="immigration">{{cite web|title=Prezidentská anketa: Jaký je váš postoj k přijímání migrantů?|url=https://www.euro.cz/prezidentske-volby-2018/prijimani-migrantu-uprchlicke-kvoty-volba-prezidenta-2018-1389328|website=Euro Portál|access-date=28 January 2018|language=cs|date=9 January 2018|trans-title=Presidential poll: What is your attitude towards accepting migrants?}}</ref>

Analysts as well as politicians saw the close election results as an illustration of the deep divisions present in Czech society.<ref name="HowEuroTrump"/><ref name="Pithart">{{cite web|title=Jsme zemí dvojího lidu. Lidé z velkoměst by ten výsledek měli vzít jako varování, říká Pithart|url=https://video.aktualne.cz/dvtv/zive-zeman-zvitezil-v-prezidenstke-volbe-sledujte-special-dv/r~a9d3d658039311e8ad1e0cc47ab5f122/|website=Aktuálně.cz|publisher=Economia|access-date=29 January 2018|date=27 January 2018|trans-title=We are the country of the dual nation. People from the cities should take the result as a warning, says [[Petr Pithart|Pithart]]|language=cs}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|first=James|last=Shotter|title=Zeman's Presidential Victory Highlights Czech Divisions on EU | url=https://www.ft.com/content/2123e006-041e-11e8-9650-9c0ad2d7c5b5 | date=28 January 2018 | newspaper=[[Financial Times]] | access-date=29 January 2018}}</ref>

